apt-blitz (0.14.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * blitzctl timestamps (cache ls -l and cache info) are now rendered in
    the local timezone like GNU `ls -l`: `%b %e %H:%M` for timestamps
    within the last six months, `%b  %e  %Y` otherwise.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.14.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * blitzctl cache find accepts size and age filters. --min-size/--max-size
    take plain bytes or a k/m/g/t suffix (powers of 1024). Age filters are
    relative durations (s/m/h/d/w) applied to the two cache timestamps:
    --cached-min-age/--cached-max-age against cached_at and
    --access-min-age/--access-max-age against last_access. Following find(1)
    semantics, min_age keeps entries older than the bound and max_age keeps
    entries within it. Folders are only shown when they contain a file that
    passes all filters.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.13.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * blitzctl: add `cache cat` (print the raw streamed contents of a single
    cached file to stdout) and `cache cp` (copy a single cached file to the
    local filesystem; an existing destination directory places the file
    inside it, and overwriting an existing file requires --force). Both
    require an unambiguous exact HOST + PATH match — no glob patterns — and
    verify the copied/emitted byte count against the cached size.
  * blitzctl cache info: report file checksums (MD5, SHA1, SHA256, SHA512)
    computed on the fly from the stored file; shown as "-" when the file is
    missing or unreadable.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Wed, 09 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.12.2-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * blitzctl: rename the cache removal subcommand from `cache clear` to
    `cache rm`. No alias is kept. The full-clear confirmation prompt and
    output messages now use "removed" to match the new name.
  * Documentation: add the blitzctl cache-control section to README, ship a
    new man/blitzctl.1 man page in RPM and DEB, document
    --coalesce-etag-max-retries, and correct the FTPS and multithreaded
    connection claims in README and the apt-blitz man page.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.12.1-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * blitzctl cache ls and cache info take positional HOST and PATH
    arguments (like tree/find/clear) instead of a target/URL selector.
    HOST may be a configured url_map alias or the real upstream host; ls
    builds the listing under the matching alias/real perspective and info
    shows the entry in that perspective. Single-token or URL-style HOST
    input is rejected. info now honours the configured max_cache_age when
    reporting freshness instead of a hardcoded 86400.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0300

apt-blitz (0.12.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * blitzctl cache ls: list cached entries like the system `ls` over the
    cache URL namespace. Supports a host/path selector and glob filters,
    and the flags -l (long: cached_at, last access, seconds until expiry,
    size), --human (human-readable sizes), -R (recursive), -1 (one per
    line), and sorting by name (-N), time (-t), cache time (-c), size (-S),
    with -r to reverse. Directories are always listed first.

 -- Petr Sleptsov <spetr@bk.ru>  Mon, 24 Aug 2026 12:00:00 +0300

